  <section style="padding: 4rem 0; background: #0a0a0a;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Selection Methodology Deep Dive</h2>
      
      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">In our 27 years in Bangladesh garment manufacturing, we've seen factories come and go. The 2026 landscape reflects a changed industry: post-Accord and Alliance reforms, Bangladesh's approaching LDC graduation, EU Digital Product Passport preparation, and a growing sense that compliance now equals capability. Alongside our own sourcing experience, we drew on public certification databases, trade body statistics, and published reporting on the 2024 Red Sea shipping disruptions.</p>

      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 2rem;">Where we could, we favoured manufacturers with a track record of compliance and a diversified client base — concentration in a single client can be a real risk if that client's business changes suddenly, as some brands found during 2025 retail difficulties. Factories with more diversified client bases were weighted favourably, even where their individual order volumes were smaller.</p>

      <p style="color: #FFFFFF; line-height: 1.8;">For Bangladesh manufacturers specifically, we weighted GOTS 7.0 certification, since EU buyers are preparing for the 2027 Digital Product Passport deadline and GOTS-certified factories tend to have traceability systems already in place. General industry context in this guide draws on <a href="https://www.bgmea.com.bd/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">BGMEA</a> production statistics and <a href="https://betterwork.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">ILO Better Work</a> program reports.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SCHEMA_PLACEHOLDER: ItemList + Article + BreadcrumbList + FAQPage -->

  <section style="padding: 4rem 0;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 500; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 2rem;">The Ranking: Top 50 Clothing Manufacturers Worldwide</h2>

      <!-- #1 SDF CLOTHING -->
      <div style="border: 1px solid #e00; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0a0a0a 0%, #000 100%);">
        <p style="font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">#1 — Bangladesh · This is us</p>
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 600; color: #fff; margin-bottom: 1rem;">SDF Clothing</h3>
        
        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Founded in 1998, SDF Clothing has grown from a small workshop into a full-service garment factory in Dhaka's Baridhara DOHS. Our 28-year history through Bangladesh's RMG evolution — from pre-Accord days to post-2023 reforms — shapes how we work with buyers today. We specialize in knitwear with a 300-piece MOQ, making us one of the more accessible Bangladesh manufacturers for startup fashion brands. Our GOTS 7.0 certification (valid through 2026) positions us for EU Digital Product Passport compliance, while our OEKO-TEX Standard 100 covers CPSIA requirements for US children's wear.</p>

        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">What we focus on beyond certifications is a full-service OEM approach. We handle fabric sourcing (GOTS-certified organic cotton from partner mills), pattern making, sampling, and production under one roof. This reduces communication overhead for buyers, especially first-timers who don't have established supply chains. Our typical lead time is 20-45 days depending on complexity, shipping primarily through Chittagong and Mongla ports.</p>

        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">We're transparent about our limitations: we're not a mass-market factory, and we don't handle complex woven garments or outerwear — those require specialized machinery we don't have. Our sweet spot is knitwear for EU, <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-uk/" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">UK</a>, USA, and Australia brands with 300-10,000 piece orders. Our pricing is mid-range for Bangladesh — we're not the cheapest (that's difficult with a 300-piece MOQ and GOTS certification), but we aim to offer value through reliability and technical support.</p>

        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">Ideal buyer match: Startup fashion brands launching first collections, boutique labels needing 300-1,000 piece runs, sustainable brands requiring GOTS certification, and buyers who value communication over rock-bottom pricing. Not ideal for: Mass-market brands needing 50,000+ piece runs, brands requiring complex woven garments or outerwear, buyers seeking the absolute lowest FOB price regardless of compliance. Use our <a href="/tools/moq-calculator/" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">MOQ calculator</a> to estimate costs for your order size.</p>

        <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(150px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid #1a1a1a;">
          <div><p style="font-size: 0.65rem; color: #FFFFFF; margin-bottom: 0.25rem;">Founded</p><p style="color: #fff; font-size: 0.85rem;">1998</p></div>
